---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Seal from '../components/Seal.astro';
import SystemMap from '../components/SystemMap.astro';
import { EVIDENCE, DEPTH } from '../lib/labels';
import { conditionsInOrder, problemsInOrder, statusCounts } from '../lib/content';
import { SITE, pad, url } from '../lib/site';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import figures from '../data/figures.json';
import ecosystem from '../data/ecosystem.json';

const conditions = await conditionsInOrder();
const problems = (await problemsInOrder()).slice(0, 6);
const totalProblems = (await getCollection('problems')).length;
const field = await Promise.all(
  (
    [
      ['programs', 'Programs', 'Research to find out what works, funding to act on it, training to grow the field.'],
      ['tools', 'Tools', 'Free instruments that put the method in anyone’s hands. Everything runs in your browser.'],
      ['record', 'The Record', 'What the field knows, and what it doesn’t yet, with every claim sourced and labeled.'],
    ] as const
  ).map(async ([key, title, text]) => {
    const counts = await statusCounts(key);
    const total = Object.values(counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    return { key, title, text, counts, total };
  }),
);
const giving = figures.usGiving;
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">An open science · Est. {SITE.established}</span>
        <h1 class="display">Charitology</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">The science of doing the most good.</p>
        <p class="lede">
          Americans gave <strong>${giving.billions} billion</strong> to charity in {giving.year}. The generosity is real, and so
          is the good it does. But the system that aims it, meaning the signals, incentives and habits that decide where the
          money goes, deserves careful study. Charitology brings those questions into one open project.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row hero-actions">
          <a class="btn" href={url('/diagnosis/')}>Read the diagnosis</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={url('/tools/values-compass/')}>Find your compass</a>
        </div>
        <p class="note hero-src">
          Figure: <a href={giving.sources[0].url}>{giving.sources[0].publisher}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-seal" aria-hidden="true">
        <Seal id="hero-seal" size={300} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section discovery">
    <div class="wrap discovery-grid">
      <div class="ten">$10</div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The ten-dollar discovery</span>
        <h2>A ten-dollar beginning, and an open invitation</h2>
        <p>
          The project’s founding story begins with <em>charitology.org</em>, registered in October {SITE.established} for about
          ten dollars. The name offered a home for an ambition: to make the system of giving easier to study, question and improve.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href={url('/diagnosis/missing-profession/')}>Research on philanthropy already exists.</a> This project adds a particular lens: follow generosity through the whole
          system, from the signals that aim it to the outcomes and feedback that should help it learn.
        </p>
        <a href={url('/manifesto/')}>Read the manifesto, “Ten Dollars” →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The subject</span>
        <h2>Charity is a system</h2>
        <p>
          Money moves from givers, through the signals they see and the channels that hold it, into work that ranges from
          relief to source, and on to outcomes. Results rarely travel back. Each pin below is a condition of the system,
          placed where it acts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <SystemMap />
      <div class="principles">
        <div>
          <h3>No judgment of the good being done</h3>
          <p>Every food bank, clinic and volunteer is doing real good. Charitology studies the system that aims them, not their hearts.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Symptoms and sources</h3>
          <p>
            Most problems keep coming back until their sources change. Charitology asks every gift where it acts, and asks
            the system whether its mix is right.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Unknown stays unknown</h3>
          <p>A science says what it doesn’t know. Every claim here is labeled established, documented, debated or hypothesis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The core instrument</span>
        <h2>From relief to source</h2>
        <p>
          Every piece of work acts somewhere on the chain from symptom to source. Depth describes the work. It never grades
          it: every level is needed. The question is always the mix.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="depth-scale">
        {
          DEPTH.map((d) => (
            <li>
              <span class={`depth-bar d${d.level}`} aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="depth-level">{d.level}</span>
              <strong>{d.name}</strong>
              <span class="depth-verb">{d.verb}</span>
              <span class="depth-ex">{d.example}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="more"><a href={url('/method/')}>The full Charitology Method →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Diagnosis</span>
        <h2>Fifteen conditions of the charity system</h2>
        <p>The subject is the system. Each condition is labeled with its evidence; hypotheses are questions to test.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="cond-grid">
        {
          conditions.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={url(`/diagnosis/${c.id}/`)}>
                <span class="numeral">C{pad(c.data.number)}</span>
                <span class="cond-title">{c.data.title}</span>
                <span class="cond-ev" title={EVIDENCE[c.data.evidence].note}>
                  <span aria-hidden="true">{EVIDENCE[c.data.evidence].glyph}</span> {EVIDENCE[c.data.evidence].label}
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section problems-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Open Problems</span>
        <h2>{totalProblems} questions nobody has answered</h2>
        <p>
          In 1900 David Hilbert’s list of 23 unsolved problems steered a century of mathematics. These are charitology’s.
          Solve one and you change where billions of dollars go.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="prob-grid">
        {
          problems.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <a href={url(`/open-problems/${p.id}/`)}>
                <span class="pnum">{pad(p.data.number)}</span>
                <span class="ptitle">{p.data.title}</span>
                <span class="pstatement">{p.data.statement}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="more"><a href={url('/open-problems/')}>All {totalProblems} open problems →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The field</span>
        <h2>Everything a science needs, built in the open</h2>
        <p>Live means the software or publication described on its page is available. Nine programs still need the people, funding and authority in their charters before they can operate as institutions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-grid">
        {
          field.map((f) => (
            <a class="card field-card" href={url(`/${f.key}/`)}>
              <span class="field-total">{f.total}</span>
              <h3>{f.title}</h3>
              <p>{f.text}</p>
              <p class="note">
                {f.counts.live} available functions · {f.counts.seeded} seeded · {f.counts.designed} designed
              </p>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Instruments already running</span>
        <h2>Open projects charitology builds on</h2>
        <p>Independent, open tools that already measure parts of the system. Charitology links them into one field.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        {
          ecosystem.instruments.map((i) => (
            <a class="card" href={i.url}>
              <span class="eyebrow eco-role">{i.role}</span>
              <h3>{i.name}</h3>
              <p>{i.summary}</p>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section join">
    <div class="wrap join-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Take part</span>
        <h2>Become a charitologist</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The field is open. Study it, question it, test it, teach it. Prove a claim wrong and make it better. Every page here
          is a file anyone can improve.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn" href={url('/contribute/')}>Start contributing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={SITE.repo}>See the source on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="roles">
        <li><strong>Researchers</strong> take on an open problem.</li>
        <li><strong>Builders</strong> ship a designed tool or program.</li>
        <li><strong>Writers</strong> grow the Record, with sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Critics</strong> red-team any claim on the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Givers</strong> try the tools and tell us what broke.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 7rem) clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 400px at 80% -10%, var(--accent-wash), transparent 70%),
      var(--bg);
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .hero-actions {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
  .hero-src {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .hero-seal {
    display: none;
    justify-self: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero-seal {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  .hero-seal :global(.seal) {
    width: min(300px, 100%);
    height: auto;
  }

  .discovery {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .discovery-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 3rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-items: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .discovery-grid {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .ten {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(5rem, 16vw, 11rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .discovery h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .discovery p {
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .principles {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr));
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .principles h3 {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .principles p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .depth-scale {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 190px), 1fr));
  }
  .depth-scale li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    align-content: start;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0 1rem 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .depth-bar {
    display: block;
    height: 8px;
    margin: 0 -1rem 0.75rem;
  }
  .depth-level {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .depth-scale strong {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 580;
  }
  .depth-verb {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .depth-ex {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .more {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .more a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cond-grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 270px), 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .cond-grid li {
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .cond-grid a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .cond-grid a:hover {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .cond-grid a:hover .cond-title {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .cond-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    font-weight: 580;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .cond-ev {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .problems-band {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .prob-grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr));
  }
  .prob-grid a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 0.2rem 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .pnum {
    grid-row: span 2;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2.1rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .ptitle {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    font-weight: 580;
  }
  .pstatement {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .prob-grid a:hover .ptitle {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .field-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
  }
  .field-total {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 3rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .field-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }
  .eco-role {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .join {
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .join-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem 4rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-items: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .join-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .join .lede {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .roles {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .roles li {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
</style>
